  "findings": [
    "For size < hashSize*1024 code disables end read but leaves read size at half original budget. With 2KiB budget, 1500-byte files differing only after byte1024 produce same digest and false duplicate, reproduced using original transpiled class.",
    "Large-file sampled edges accepted as final identity without full hash or byte verification. Equal-size 4096-byte pair with same edges but different middle falsely grouped, reproduced. SHA256 does not repair unobserved bytes.",
    "Ignores bytesRead and hashes entire zero-initialized buffer; short read or growing/shrinking file not revalidated. No identity/mutation check.",
    "Repeated same physical path counted as duplicate of itself, reproduced by original scanFile calls; traversal stat follows symlinks with no visited identity or cycle tracking. No deletion executed.",
    "processFile may unlink immediately on sampled key; delete false throughout controls with explicit unlink guard. Source only for delete path.",
    "Errors caught/logged but output end retains only duplicate groups and drops diagnostics, no complete/cancel contract. Non-file/non-directory entries treated as files; synchronous traversal blocks event loop.",
    "parallel first-observed original depends on asynchronous read completion, despite alphabetical order claims. No timing or performance qualification.",
    "Docs/help disagree with implementation defaults/units (SHA1 vs SHA256, bytes vs KiB); root MIT copyright still template placeholders. No source copying.",
    "21 whole-text reads, 7 generated markup/code/CSS/lock structural assessments and 4 raster sprite visual reviews cover all32 paths. Full manual repository read remains false; generated mainJS/CSS/rawHTML not manually read whole. Controls unchanged, no upstream suite or browser runtime."
